    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. like, if the end state of everything is just a cold, empty void, then all the struggle, the pain, and the effort we put into being \"someone\" is just a massive waste of energy. it's actually kind of irrational to keep fighting against the physics of it all. it's like trying to build a sandcastle right before the tide comes in. why keep struggling when the outcome is already mathematically certain?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
